<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salar Jung III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Mir Yousuf Ali Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salar Jung III, born Mir Yousuf Ali Khan, was a Hyderabad noble, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salar-jung-i">Salar Jung I</a>, who served briefly as prime minister of the state in 1912–1914. He spent much of his fortune collecting art, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> and objects from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, which after his death formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salar-jung-museum">Salar Jung Museum</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salar-jung-iii.jpg" alt="Salar Jung III" width="186" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rgajavelli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salarjungiii.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
